@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+## #2961 - Group two captured Agie punches
+
+Use two complete punch solids on one 20 mm plate. Each operation owns one solid, one external threading hole, and its own capture declaration. Every model in the document must have an owning operation. Both operations share one setup and wire tool. Control-generated separation can run after both profiles. Cross-work order must therefore be immaterial to clearance and capture.
+
+Compare conservative XY bounds that include the entire retained solid, the hole, the approach and return, the 3 mm lead, the largest possible rough miter, and the wire radius. A separating X or Y interval proves that every pass of one work clears the other. This can refuse some safe nested or diagonally spaced layouts. Those layouts require a more precise geometric proof.
+
+Keep both geometry files in common setup coordinates with zero work translations. Attach each resource and start point to its own WORK in one native GROUP. Create the same resident Fine Ra 0.30 quality for each work. The single-work generation and names retain their previous format. Pair names reserve one of the eight DOS filename characters for the work number. Publish the complete resource map, piece and two geometry files in one directory rename.
